comments.body:
@penfever it depends on the behavior we want, if I'm reading this correctly, it sounds like a bug in evalchemy where it's not resuming from a partial/complete run (or in finestore). It's certainly possible to ask Iris for the attempt ID an eval is being run at and create a new output, but I suspect we want to fix the resumption instead.

@weaverbot can you investigate marin-community/evalchemy and/or finestore restore and see if this is a bug there?

> s3://marin-us-east-02a/marin/evals/20260930-085011-arcee-ai-Trinity-Mini-nupa-9a91/results held a sealed 5,000-item attempt with 2,414 correct answers (0.4828). Iris classified the completed Evalchemy child attempt as WORKER_FAILED after PodDeleted, retried the same task and path, and the final canonical record became 0.4788.

this one seems suspicious - pod retries are expected and should be tolerated - the evalchemy child should have simply skipped the rerun if the previous run was actually finished.

Will's #9813 will fix a bulk of these issues as well - that makes gives every finished eval an atomic "done" indicator independent of evalchemy/harbor.
